WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.678
This would be easier with
a serrated knife I think.

00:00:02.678 --> 00:00:03.524
A what knife?

00:00:03.524 --> 00:00:05.253
(laughter)

00:00:05.253 --> 00:00:08.615
(playful music)

00:00:08.615 --> 00:00:11.199
Personally I love turkey.
I only eat poultry,

00:00:11.199 --> 00:00:12.654
so I only chicken and turkey.

00:00:12.654 --> 00:00:13.963
I think drumstick is definitely

00:00:13.963 --> 00:00:17.438
my favorite part of the
turkey and there's only two,

00:00:17.438 --> 00:00:20.091
so that's like it's a
very competitive thing.

00:00:20.091 --> 00:00:24.081
I have zero cooking ability
and zero cooking experience.

00:00:24.081 --> 00:00:27.976
I probably learned how to
boil water at a very old age.

00:00:27.976 --> 00:00:30.047
That's sort of embarrassing to admit.

00:00:30.047 --> 00:00:34.214
I just learned how to cut
an onion the other day.

00:00:35.698 --> 00:00:40.161
When I was a freshman in
college, so when I was like 18.

00:00:40.161 --> 00:00:41.141
I would say I'm the person that

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:45.059
kind of just shows up on Thanksgiving.

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:48.568
I have never carved a
turkey in my entire life.

00:00:48.568 --> 00:00:50.354
(intense music)

00:00:50.354 --> 00:00:53.104
(turkey gobbles)

00:00:54.799 --> 00:00:57.299
Uh oh, I knew it. I knew it.

00:01:00.921 --> 00:01:01.981
It's a trap.

00:01:01.981 --> 00:01:02.814
It's always a trap.

00:01:02.814 --> 00:01:03.647
Damn it.

00:01:06.739 --> 00:01:08.405
(intense music)

00:01:08.405 --> 00:01:09.488
I don't know.

00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:13.236
Do we get a knife?

00:01:13.236 --> 00:01:15.464
(energetic music)

00:01:15.464 --> 00:01:19.495
Okay, so wait, what's our
game plan here? Middle?

00:01:19.495 --> 00:01:20.947
So have you ever carved a turkey before?

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.028
No.

00:01:22.028 --> 00:01:23.397
So this is your first time?

00:01:23.397 --> 00:01:24.230
Yes.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:25.121
And I'm a part of it?

00:01:25.121 --> 00:01:25.954
Yes.

00:01:25.954 --> 00:01:28.947
Gotta angle it. This is really awkward.

00:01:28.947 --> 00:01:31.065
Wait, I think it would work
with left-handed actually.

00:01:31.065 --> 00:01:32.420
You're doing a great job.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.520
Thanks. You're doing a
great job too, of eating.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.595
But the leg gets in the way.

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:38.850
Do you cut the leg out
of the way first maybe?

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.350
Oh yeah! Cut the legs out.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.909
I think you have a little
bit of turkey in your hair.

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:43.294
Oh my God, I do?

00:01:43.294 --> 00:01:44.127
Yeah.

00:01:44.127 --> 00:01:45.433
Oh my God.

00:01:45.433 --> 00:01:49.161
Oh my gosh, why is it
tied? There's string.

00:01:49.161 --> 00:01:50.469
Do people usually do this?

00:01:50.469 --> 00:01:51.969
S and M bondage.

00:01:52.877 --> 00:01:54.031
(nervous laughter)

00:01:54.031 --> 00:01:55.599
Should we have cut it over?

00:01:55.599 --> 00:01:58.225
No, I don't think that's a thing.

00:01:58.225 --> 00:01:59.058
(shouts)

00:01:59.058 --> 00:02:00.051
It's like Disneyland.

00:02:00.051 --> 00:02:00.884
Yeah.

00:02:00.884 --> 00:02:01.892
Should we turn the plate around,

00:02:01.892 --> 00:02:03.097
so you can do the other side?

00:02:03.097 --> 00:02:04.715
I think you should do the other side.

00:02:04.715 --> 00:02:05.840
I don't think anyone will show up

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.007
to our Thanksgiving party.

00:02:10.626 --> 00:02:11.726
I'd feel better.
Yes please!

00:02:11.726 --> 00:02:13.412
That'd be great. I'd
feel like he'd be like,

00:02:13.412 --> 00:02:17.951
"you guys did a great
job". Cause look, we did.

00:02:17.951 --> 00:02:19.558
We did.

00:02:19.558 --> 00:02:22.824
(folksy music)

00:02:22.824 --> 00:02:25.496
Cut down to the thigh. Have the legs

00:02:25.496 --> 00:02:27.510
be pushed down by the wings.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.656
That looks very different
from when we were doing it.

00:02:29.656 --> 00:02:32.923
(folksy music)

00:02:32.923 --> 00:02:34.758
The thigh bone, since it's cooked well,

00:02:34.758 --> 00:02:38.471
should come off really
easily. It's nice and tender.

00:02:38.471 --> 00:02:41.778
(folksy music)

00:02:41.778 --> 00:02:45.729
So you're gonna cut off the
turkey breast, right here.

00:02:45.729 --> 00:02:47.126
So we've got one breast there,

00:02:47.126 --> 00:02:50.378
Oh that's nice.
and then cut down here.

00:02:50.378 --> 00:02:51.610
Yeah, we didn't do that.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.937
(folksy music)

00:02:54.937 --> 00:02:59.104
You can see that it just
comes open at the joint there,

00:03:00.018 --> 00:03:02.617
and you can tear it or
you can find the joint

00:03:02.617 --> 00:03:04.637
and then you can just kinda cut it.

00:03:04.637 --> 00:03:07.867
(folksy music)

00:03:07.867 --> 00:03:09.138
What you wanna do is
you actually wanna cut

00:03:09.138 --> 00:03:11.809
against the grain. So if you see here.

00:03:11.809 --> 00:03:14.480
Now you've got your
beautifully carved turkey.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.988
That looks--
It's pretty.

00:03:15.988 --> 00:03:16.821
- [Both] Yeah.

00:03:16.821 --> 00:03:18.756
Now we're gonna go with the drumstick.

00:03:18.756 --> 00:03:20.968
What you wanna do is
you wanna find the joint

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:23.200
and then all you have to do is tear it.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.271
Then, what you wanna do with the thigh,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.922
you can just kinda take it out,

00:03:27.922 --> 00:03:32.043
and now you can flip it
over and cut the thigh meat.

00:03:32.043 --> 00:03:33.880
So, there you go.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.694
See, you make this look so easy.

00:03:35.694 --> 00:03:37.156
Okay, I thought we did a pretty good job,

00:03:37.156 --> 00:03:39.672
but it is become apparent
to me that we did not.

00:03:39.672 --> 00:03:43.511
I mean, I feel like, yeah we didn't.

00:03:43.511 --> 00:03:45.400
(playful music)

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.259
This turkey carving experience,

00:03:48.259 --> 00:03:50.671
I definitely feel like
I can brag to my family

00:03:50.671 --> 00:03:52.571
now that I know how to carve a turkey.

00:03:52.571 --> 00:03:54.529
I definitely didn't think there was

00:03:54.529 --> 00:03:57.237
as much to it as there is.

00:03:57.237 --> 00:04:01.404
Our only strategy going
into the carving process was

00:04:02.293 --> 00:04:04.025
make it edible.

00:04:04.025 --> 00:04:06.586
I mean, regardless of how
it's carved, I'm gonna eat it.

00:04:06.586 --> 00:04:09.495
I do definitely have a
greater appreciation for

00:04:09.495 --> 00:04:11.897
turkey carvers. It is art.

00:04:11.897 --> 00:04:13.693
Every single turkey that I've seen carved,

00:04:13.693 --> 00:04:15.745
even though I wasn't really
paying full attention,

00:04:15.745 --> 00:04:19.175
didn't seem to look anything
like how Vaughn just showed us.

00:04:19.175 --> 00:04:22.094
I don't think this has
inspired me to cook.

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:24.064
I think if anything it has deterred me.

00:04:24.064 --> 00:04:26.295
I think I'll just stick to the microwave.

00:04:26.295 --> 00:04:29.725
(playful music)

00:04:29.725 --> 00:04:32.572
Anything with green, like sage,

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:36.332
would be really good here, or rosemary.

00:04:36.332 --> 00:04:37.265
We've got--

00:04:37.265 --> 00:04:38.365
Cilantro?

00:04:38.365 --> 00:04:39.865
This is parsley.

